qspacemidi (1.0.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Detect 3D mice again on Windows: the raw HID backend looked for a
    vendor-defined top-level collection, which no 3Dconnexion device
    actually exposes, so the mouse was never found.  Match the Generic
    Desktop / Multi-Axis Controller collection instead and verify that it
    declares the six axes.
  * Decode the input reports through HidP_* rather than fixed byte offsets,
    so both the wired SpaceNavigator, which splits translation and rotation
    over two reports, and the wireless models, which pack all six axes into
    one, are read correctly.
  * Take the axis range from the report descriptor on Windows instead of
    assuming +-512 and +-900, so full deflection reaches full scale.
  * Emit the axis signals from the Windows and macOS backends, without
    which the meters never moved and no MIDI was sent.
  * Show the product name of the device instead of its raw HID path.

 -- Jakob Flierl <jakob.flierl@gmail.com>  Mon, 10 Aug 2026 18:00:00 +0200

